Scenario: CSE CN Routing for FLS Organizations
	End users who create requests for a China support organization with partner first line support for specific products and components should have their requests routed to the BCP Management group.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status                     | Approved            |
	| Name                       | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags                       | liferay_portal      |
	| Shared Tickets             | true                |
	| Shared Comments            | true                |
	| SLA                        | Gold                |
	| Tier                       | T4                  |
	| Support Region             | China               |
	| Support Language           | Chinese             |
	| Partner First Line Support | true                |
	| External ID                | 12345678            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | Chinese                          |
	| Time Zone        | Beijing                          |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | patch_management |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to the group "BCP Management"

Scenario: CSE AU Routing for FLS Organizations
	End users who create requests for an Australia support organization with partner first line support for specific products and components should have their requests routed to the BCP Management group.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status                     | Approved            |
	| Name                       | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags                       | liferay_portal      |
	| Shared Tickets             | true                |
	| Shared Comments            | true                |
	| SLA                        | Gold                |
	| Tier                       | T4                  |
	| Support Region             | Australia           |
	| Support Language           | English             |
	| Partner First Line Support | true                |
	| External ID                | 12345678            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Sydney                           | 
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | patch_management |
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should be assigned to either the group "CSE - AU" or "BCP Management"

